      "worked_solution": "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=6$ and $r=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{2}) & =\\frac{6!}{(6-2)!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4!}{4!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{\\cancel{4!}\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{2} \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
